<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">North Cape</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nordkapp</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The North Cape, or Nordkapp, is a cliff on the island of Magerøya in Finnmark, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, often described as the northernmost point of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Around 890 the Hålogaland chieftain Ohthere sailed round it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-sea">White Sea</a> and described the voyage to King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred of Wessex</a>. It received its English name from an English expedition in 1553.</p></div>
